// Marionette plans Marionette (G5): the trajectory from the Phase 1 toolchain
// landing through the end of Phase 2. Node metadata carries GitHub mapping
// stubs (github:issue) so each phase can be linked to an issue when filed.
# project: marionette
# github:repo: leemeichin/marionette
VAR skill_revisions = 0

-> phase1_toolchain

=== phase1_toolchain ===
Land the Phase 1 toolchain: DSL compiler, structural validation, gate checking,
Mermaid render, plan summaries, hash-bound state with drift detection, CLI and
test suite. (P0.1–P0.4, P0.6–P0.8)
# github:pr: 1
* [PR merged, CI green] -> authoring_skill
+ [Review requested changes] ~loop~ -> phase1_toolchain

=== authoring_skill ===
Build the NL → draft-script authoring skill (P0.5): project notes in, a
compilable .mar out, with compiler errors surfaced for one revision loop.
# github:issue: 2
~ skill_revisions += 1
* [First-session compile success at or above 70%] -> dogfood_gate
+ {skill_revisions < 5} [Below the bar, iterate on prompts] ~loop~ -> authoring_skill
* {skill_revisions >= 5} [Not converging after five revisions] @human -> rethink_authoring

=== rethink_authoring ===
Five skill revisions without hitting the bar means the approach is wrong, not
the prompts. Decide a new authoring strategy with fresh constraints.
+ [New approach chosen] @human ~loop~ -> authoring_skill
+ [Ship syntax-first, defer the skill] @human -> dogfood_gate

=== dogfood_gate ===
Phase 1 exit gate (G5): Marionette's own Phase 2 is planned in Marionette, and
a reviewer with no DSL knowledge understands the rendered plan in under five
minutes.
* [Phase 1 exit approved] @human -> phase2_runtime
+ [Plan not legible enough, revise] @human ~loop~ -> authoring_skill

=== phase2_runtime ===
Reference runtime (P1): grow the minimal walker in src/state.ts into a full
graph walker and gate evaluator consuming trajectory JSON, with a decision log
recording actor, timestamp and rationale for every branch.
# github:issue: 3
* [Walker passes conformance tests] -> escalation_protocol

=== escalation_protocol ===
Resolve OQ2 — the @human escalation protocol (channel, payload, timeout and
fallback semantics) — then wire the pi agent proving ground to ingest and
traverse compiled trajectories.
# github:issue: 4
* [Protocol decided and implemented] @human -> phase2_gate

=== phase2_gate ===
Phase 2 exit gate (G2): the pi agent completes a trajectory of fifteen or more
nodes with at least one loop and one @human escalation, zero out-of-graph
actions, and rationale logged on every taken branch.
* [G2 met] @human -> END
+ [Runtime gaps found] ~loop~ -> phase2_runtime
